# Vanessa Automation Run Policy

> RULES — mandatory requirements for when a Vanessa run is required and what should be considered the minimum level of result verification.

## Purpose

This rule fixes when an agent is obligated to run a scenario and which artifacts it must check after the execution.

## Trigger conditions

The rule applies when the agent:

- created a new `.feature`;
- modified an existing `.feature`;
- changed Vanessa launch parameters;
- changed the baseline `bddRunner.epf` or the launch path.

## MUST

| Requirement | Description |
|------------|----------|
| Mandatory run | After a scenario change the agent MUST execute the scenario run |
| Mandatory artifact analysis | After the run the agent MUST check `va-status.json` and `vanessa-execution.log` |
| Mandatory event log analysis | After the run the agent MUST check `event-log` if the scenario failed or the execution looks suspicious |
| Explicit classification | On failure the agent MUST return an error class rather than just the failure text |

## Success indicator

Minimum success indicator:

1. the `va-status.json` file exists;
2. the value in `va-status.json` equals `0`;
3. the `vanessa-execution.log` file was created.

The detailed execution and diagnostics procedure is described by the skills, not by this rule.

